(B2) How to generate fxye (PWDR) files of in-situ HEXRD dataset
Load IMG files as a zip file (zip file should not located at the same folder with IMG files)
Here, you can select the stride. every 2 or every 10.. can reduce the # of dataset
Set Inner/Outer 2-theta
Click Show integration limits?, Do full integration?, Use for all new images?
Image Controls - Load Parm as cali file - Copy control
Image Controls - Integration - integrate all
Export - Powder data as - GSAS fxye file

(B3) 1D histogram fitting (no phase input)
Before Rietveld refinement for single data, it is good to check 1D histogram fitting for fxye PWDR single data
  This is to check whether the calibration has been done well
Load Sample param from cali, do Background - Peak List - fitting unit inst.param., unit cell list (same as line 16)

(C1) Single refinement (single PWDR (fxye) data)
Load phases (cif), set constraints equation (CONST 0:0Scale + 1:0Scale + 2:0Scale = 1.0)
  Constraints - Select tab - Histogram/Phase - Edit Constr./Add constraint equation - Filter: put "scale"
  Select first phase (0:0:Scale), OK, select all phases (all:0:Scale), OK
    This is to set the sum of phase fractions is always 1
Phase - General - check Refine unit cell, Phase - Data- check Use Histogram, phase fraction
Load PWDR (Import - Powder data - from GSAS powder data file), no load for background (just check Refine, no coeff 6), 
no load for instrument para (just check 5 para),
just load Sample Parameters from cali file, then Calculate - Refine
Follow 4 steps for single refinement in https://advancedphotonsource.github.io/GSAS-II-tutorials/SeqRefine/SequentialTutorial.htm
  Starting from Step I - 4. Initial fit to Step III
Iterate single refinement until chi^2 does not decrease more

(C2) How to import fxye files
"No need" to delete phase entry
Import - GSAS PWDR fxye files - select all the fxye files (do not make zip)
Once a window appears, press Tab + Enter, then it works (phase reflected)
if histogram not added, phase select - Edit Phase - Add powder histogram
Phase - data - Copy data to all the fxye dataset (while Refine cell and phase fraction, D11 checked; depending on which parameters you want)
Follow (C3) Sequential refinement

(C3) Sequential refinement
You can do Rietveld refinement for hundreds of dataset by single-click
Follow all the steps in: https://advancedphotonsource.github.io/GSAS-II-tutorials/SeqRefine/SequentialTutorial.htm
  Starting from Step IV - 2. Duplicate information across histograms
It is recommended to save the GSAS-II file into new name (e.g., xxx-1) before doing calculation, 
because if the sequential refinement fails, we need to retry all the settings again

*Errors*
Problem #1. Calculate - refine) phase 0 invalid metric tensor error
Solution #1. Set austenite fraction 0.9, ferrite 0.05, cementite 0.05 (close to the real value; all refine checked)
Problem #2. Sometimes, Sequential refinement can halt even though Rwp value is good (9-10%)
Solution #2. Check the name of GSAS-II file. If it overlaps with previous one or if the name has been changed, the calculation can be stuck
